s plan with includeTeeReplacementState=true. elementIds contains only surviving main/secondMain/branch and the new bridge/takeoff; replacementRemovedIds contains the deleted tee and actual parent-bound centerlines, replacementTypeIds the retained type scope, and preservationScheduleIds the regular schedules. The current read must establish absence, reciprocal fitted connections, span and retained parameters/types/system/schedules. Dependent annotations and any unexplained owner still cause rollback. The addition-only graph proof is insufficient; do not repeat the replacement for verification. Connect one retained branch to the interior of an existing rigid main without replacing accepted geometry. connectionMode:takeoff_fitting creates a native takeoff between one exact open rigid/flex duct or pipe connector and its main, accepts an explicit worksetId/worksetName, and otherwise inherits the retained branch user workset with committed readback. connectionMode:air_terminal_on_duct uses Revit's direct air-terminal attachment operation, requires kind:duct plus an exact open air-terminal connector, and produces the native direct terminal-to-duct topology without an adapter curve. Both modes guard the active model and projected interior point, preserve pre-existing physical connections, verify the result after transaction commit, and perform the real operation inside a rollback-verified transaction group during dry-run. Body: {expectedModelPath?,connectionMode?:takeoff_fitting|air_terminal_on_duct,kind:duct|pipe,mainElementId,branchElementId,branchConnectorId?,expectedBranchOriginXyz?,originToleranceFt?,expectedTakeoffTypeId?,expectedTakeoffFamilyName?,expectedTakeoffTypeName?,worksetId?,worksetName?,dryRun?,verify?}.",
